        "refuted": true,
        "recommendedTier": "documented",
        "sourceCheck": "partially",
        "denialFound": "OSF challenged the listing in court rather than denying it. OSF filed W.P.(C) 238/2020 in the Delhi HC in January 2020. It challenges the unpublished MHA/RBI circulars of 15.01.2015 and 07.06.2016 on two grounds: they were not notified in the Gazette as required by s.11(3)/46, and they reach remittances that are not foreign contribution. It also asked for the reasons for the listing and why no prior notice was given. OSF spokesperson Jonathan Birchall told The Hindu: \"The Open Society Foundations confirm the filing of a petition in the Delhi High Court ... will be making no further statement on the matter\" (https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/george-soros-open-society-foundations-moves-hc-against-mha/article61638640.ece). MHA's stated ground, from its affidavit: \"incriminating reports from security agencies against the Open Society Foundation, which impinges on the our national security\"; the material was filed in a sealed envelope. The case was still pending on 06.01.2026 (https://indiankanoon.org/doc/185169269/). The court asked the Union to say whether the circulars apply only to FCRA-covered remittances and listed the matter for 15.04.2026. I did not find an OSF statement on the 2025 ED searches; my web search budget was exhausted, so this is not a finding that none exists.",
        "innocentReading": "This is a routine use of s.46 FCRA, which MHA has applied to about 21 foreign donors across both governments, including two other US democracy-promotion funders in the same order. The practical effect is that each remittance to an Indian association needs MHA clearance; it is not a ban. MHA says the trigger was intelligence input. The Hindu (2016) reports the alleged conduct as funding associations not registered under FCRA. No court has tested either the ground or the listing.",
        "reason": "The underlying fact stands, but the claim's stated evidentiary position is false, and the tier depends on that position. The claim says the listing is \"known only via ED's 2025 account; the order and stated ground not opened\". In fact, (1) The Hindu reported it on 2016-06-09 with the co-listed donors and the \"adverse intelligence inputs\" ground. (2) A Delhi HC order dated 21.02.2023 in OSI v Union of India, W.P.(C) 238/2020, quotes the RBI letter of 07.06.2016 citing the MHA decision under s.46 and the MHA affidavit giving the date (30.05.2016) and the ground (\"incriminating reports from security agencies ... national security\"). (3) OSF confirmed its challenge on the record in 2020. A court order plus two independent credible outlets (The Hindu 2016 and TOI/Tribune 2025) meets the documented tier. The 'reported' tier and the \"only via ED\" framing should go, and the existing gap entry is closed by these sources.",
        "corrections": [
          "1. Change tier from reported to documented.\n2. Replace text/d with: \"MHA, by letter to RBI dated 2016-05-30 under s.46 FCRA 2010, directed that remittances from 'Open Society Foundation (OSF) ... USA' (with NED and WMD) be credited only after MHA clearance; RBI relayed this to banks on 2016-06-07 (DBR.AML.No.15320/14.08.001/2015-16). MHA's stated ground (affidavit in Delhi HC W.P.(C) 238/2020): 'incriminating reports from security agencies ... impinges on national security', with material in a sealed envelope. OSF (as Open Society Institute, with OSF London and FPOS) has challenged the circulars since January 2020 as unpublished and over-broad; the case was pending as of 2026-01-06.\"\n3. Set from = \"2016-05-30\".\n4. Add sources: https://indiankanoon.org/doc/167147408/ (DHC order 21.02.2023); https://indiankanoon.org/doc/185169269/ (DHC order 06.01.2026); https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/Three-American-donors-put-under-watch-list/article14392124.ece (2016-06-09); https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/george-soros-open-society-foundations-moves-hc-against-mha/article61638640.ece; TOI 2025-03-19 https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/ed-searches-bengaluru-offices-of-soross-foundation-and-entities-linked-to-it/articleshow/119185811.cms. Keep the Tribune but note that it misnames the entity as \"Open Source Foundation\".\n5. Add innocentReading: \"one of ~21 donors under s.46 prior reference (8 under UPA, 13 under NDA); NED and WMD were listed in the same order.\"\n6. Add contra/response: OSF's pending Delhi HC petition and the Birchall statement.\n7. Change killIf to \"Delhi HC quashes the 2016 circulars or MHA withdraws the listing\". Change upgradeIf to \"the 30.05.2016 MHA letter itself is released, or the DHC reaches a final judgment\".\n8. Follow-on fixes in the same file: close the gap entry \"2016 MHA order ... not found; known only through ED's 2025 account and a 2020 Delhi HC petition reported by a partisan outlet\". The petition is in the DHC record and was reported by The Hindu, not only by a partisan outlet. Also change \"(reported)\" to \"(documented)\" in the OSF entity 'sub', 'publicRole' and facts, and in the Soros narrative strongestCase."
        ],
