        "denialFound": "A response exists, so c016's text is wrong. On 2025-08-21 MEA told Parliament, citing US Embassy data, that USAID gave no US$21m for voter turnout in India. My recollection is that this was a written Rajya Sabha answer by MoS Kirti Vardhan Singh, which said the Embassy's 2014-2024 USAID data showed no US$21m received and no voter-turnout activity implemented. I confirmed the event only from Google News RSS listings dated 2025-08-21/22. These headlines include the Indian Express (\"Citing US embassy, Govt confirms: No $21-million USAID poll grant in India\"), The Hindu (\"USAID didn't receive funding of $21 million for voter turnout in India: Embassy to MEA\"), NDTV (\"US Embassy Contradicts Trump's 'USAID Fund For Voter Turnout In India' Claim\"), The Wire (\"MEA Says US Embassy Denies Trump's Claim of $21m USAID Funds to Modi, All USAID Pacts with India Ended August 15\"), Scroll, TOI and BOOM. I could not open the article bodies (The Wire renders with JS; Google News links are encoded), so the MoS name and the 2014-2024 window are unconfirmed. Earlier, ThePrint (2025-03-17) reported that MEA had asked the US Embassy for details. The Washington Post (2025-02-22) called it \"a false DOGE claim\". I found no statement from CEPPS, IFES, IRI or NDI themselves; whether they were asked is unknown.",
