          "1. Claim text and d: delete \"the '83%' figure is from secondary summaries, not verified in the primary text\". Replace it with a note that §4.1 of the primary text republished by Outlook gives \">80% of IDRF-designated funds to Parivar organisations (RSS, VHP, VKA)\" and \"83% … Sangh affiliated\". Flag that it is unclear whether the 83% is a share of organisations or of funds; Figure 2 is titled \"Percentage Distribution of IDRF Funds By Ideology\". 2. d: replace \"Amount not stated\" with: \"IDRF-designated disbursements 1994–2000: 'roughly 75% of the IDRF's total disbursements (over $3.2 million)'\". Note that the parenthetical could refer to either the 75% slice or the total. 3. Scope: change \"IDRF disbursements went predominantly\" to \"IDRF-designated disbursements (~75% of total) went >80% to Sangh affiliates; donor-designated only 10% (report's coding, Appendix H)\". Also record IDRF's 10% allocation to VKA on donor-designated gifts of $1,000 or more. 4. Recipient list in d: VKA, RSS and VHP affiliates in §4.1; Sewa Bharati, Ekal Vidyalaya and Bharat Kalyan Pratisthan (~$86,000) in §4.2–4.4. 5. Fill innocentReading with the lawful same-network service-funding reading above. 6. c024 contra: add the HVK summary sentence showing the rebuttal concedes the flow and disputes the \"funds violence\" characterisation; the contra URL can point to https://hvk.org/specialreports/hate/1.html. 7. File-level: update the gap at ~line 2173–2174 (\"Narrative 6's numerators (83% …) are recorded from secondary readings only\"), narrative 6's strongestCounter (\"The 83% figure is unverified here\") and the gaps list line ~2439. The 83% is now read in the primary text via Outlook; only its scope (organisations vs funds) is unresolved. 8. Optional: consider an ngo:vka target node instead of or alongside the collective \"rss\" node. benefit.amountCr stays null unless a dated USD→INR conversion is recorded."
