        "denialFound": "Yes. Oxfam India said it \"is fully compliant with Indian laws and has filed all its statutory compliances, including Foreign Contribution Regulation Act (FCRA) returns, in a timely manner since its inception\", and that it has \"been cooperating with all government agencies since its FCRA registration wasn't renewed in December 2021\". Sources: CIVICUS 2023-04-20 https://www.civicus.org/index.php/media-resources/news/6370-india-oxfam-targeted-again-with-accusations-of-foreign-funding-and-influencing and The Week 2025-01-23 https://www.theweek.in/news/india/2025/01/23/cbi-files-charge-sheet-against-oxfam-india-for-violating-fcra-norms.html. This is recorded as contra c050. Neither cited source gives the statement's date as 2023-04-06.",
        "innocentReading": "The \"pressure via foreign governments\" allegation fits ordinary advocacy: an affiliate of an international confederation asks its partners and donor governments to raise its licence refusal. That is lobbying, not an offence in itself; the MHA's own framing is \"has the reach and influence to request multilateral foreign organisations to intervene\". Funds received after 2022-01-01 may be remittances already committed or in transit that sat in the FCRA account. Sub-grants after the 2020 Amendment may have honoured commitments made before it, while the scope of the ban was unsettled until the Supreme Court's 2022-04-08 ruling. The 2013–2016 routing may be a procedural or accounting lapse, the kind of ground often compounded under Section 41 rather than prosecuted. Two things cannot be tested from the evidence in hand: the trial is pending, and no court has made a finding.",
        "reason": "Both source URLs say what the claim says, and I quoted them. CIVICUS carries the FIR date (2023-04-19) and all four allegations: pressure via foreign governments and institutions, receipt of funds after cessation, sub-grants after the 2020 ban, and designated-account circumvention in 2013–2016. The Week carries the chargesheet date (2025-01-23, special court, Delhi), the pressure allegation and the \"structure to continue its operations with foreign funds\" allegation. The dates line up, the entity is the one the sources name, and the response is on record as a linked contra. \"Alleged\" is the right tier for the content: the FIR and chargesheet are two independently reported facts, but what they assert has not been decided. I found nothing that refutes the claim. Caveat: my web-search budget was exhausted, so I could not check for any court development after 2025-01 (cognizance, discharge, quash).",
